<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:chol/shacharit/pesukei_dezimra/hoshia_et_amekha">
<tei:p>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/28/9"/>Save thy people and bless thy heritage; tend them and sustain them forever.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/33/20"/>Our soul waits for the Lord; he is our help and our shield.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/33/21"/>Indeed, our heart rejoices in him, for in his holy name we trust.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/33/22"/>May thy kindness, O Lord, rest on us, as our hope rests on thee.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/85/8"/>Show us thy kindness, O Lord, and grant us thy salvation.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/44/27"/>Arise for our help, and set us free for thy goodness’ sake.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/81/11"/>I am the Lord your God, who brought you up from the land of Egypt; open your mouth and I will fill it.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/144/15"/>Happy the people that is so situated; happy the people whose God is the Lord.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/13/6"/>I have trusted in thy kindness; may my heart rejoice in thy salvation; I will sing to the Lord, because he has treated me kindly.
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
</tei:p>
</tei:div>
